.TH ALARMQT 1 "October 2026" "alarmqt" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
alarmqt \- keyboard-friendly system-tray alarms and reminders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B alarmqt
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIALARM\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B alarmqt
is a small Qt6 system-tray alarm application for Linux.
It accepts relative times (for example
.Qq in 5m )
and absolute times (for example
.Qq at 15:10 ),
optionally with a short human-readable note.
Alarms keep notifying (dialog, tray message, and sound) until they are
acknowledged or snoozed.
.PP
Only one instance runs at a time.
A second invocation talks to the running process over the session D-Bus
(raise the window, add an alarm, list, quit, and so on).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the full version string and exit.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quit
Quit the running instance.
If none is running, exit successfully without starting the GUI.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List alarms.
If no instance is running, print the stored list and exit without starting
the GUI.
If an instance is running, query it over D-Bus and print the reply.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-raise
Raise the existing main window.
.SH ALARM EXPRESSIONS
.SS Relative
.BR in\ 5m ,
.BR in\ 2h30m ,
.BR in\ 1d ,
.BR in\ 2\ weeks ,
.BR in\ 1\ month ,
.BR 5m ,
.BR 30s
.SS Absolute
.BR at\ 15:10 ,
.BR at\ 2026\-10\-03\ 09:00 ,
.BR 15:10 ,
.BR 6:00pm ,
.BR 6am
(next occurrence if that clock time has already passed today)
.PP
.BR today\ 17:00 ,
.BR tomorrow\ 9:00 ,
.BR tomorrow\ noon
— today or tomorrow at the given local time.
.PP
.BR next\ monday\ 5:50pm ,
.BR monday\ 9:00 ,
.BR next\ mon\ at\ 9:00
— the next matching weekday at that local wall-clock time (not a repeating
alarm). Leading
.B next
is optional. Day names may be short or full; optional
.BR at
before the time.
.PP
.BR noon
and
.B midnight
are accepted as times (12:00 and 00:00). Full dates accept am/pm:
.BR at\ 2026\-10\-06\ 5:00pm .
.PP
Optional
.B glued
timezone on absolute times (no space before the zone; a space starts the note):
.BR at\ 15:10CEST ,
.BR at\ 12:00Z ,
.BR at\ 15:10+02:00 ,
.BR at\ 15:10CEST\ ship\ it .
Spaced names are labels:
.B at 15:10 CEST
uses the system zone and the label CEST.
.SS Repeating
.TP
.BR every\ 5m ,\ every\ 1h30m ,\ every\ hour
Interval alarm. After it is acknowledged it fires again after the interval,
counted from the acknowledgement; an ignored alarm stays due instead of
queueing more.
.TP
.BR every\ monday\ at\ 18:00 ,\ every\ mon,\ thu\ 6pm
Weekly alarm at a local wall-clock time; it stays at that time across
daylight-saving changes. Days may be full or short names, plural, and joined
with commas,
.BR and ,
.B &
or
.BR / .
.TP
.BR daily\ at\ 7:30 ,\ every\ day\ at\ 7:30 ,\ every\ weekday\ at\ 9:00 ,\ weekends\ 10am
Every day, Monday to Friday, or Saturday and Sunday.
.TP
.BR every\ month\ on\ the\ 6th\ at\ 9:00 ,\ monthly\ on\ 15\ at\ 18:00
Monthly at a local wall-clock time on the given day of the month.
Months that do not have that day (for example the 31st in February) are
skipped. Ordinal suffixes
.RB ( st ,\ nd ,\ rd ,\ th )
are optional.
.PP
.B each
is accepted in place of
.BR every ;
.B monthly
is accepted in place of
.BR every\ month .
Acknowledging a repeating alarm schedules its next occurrence instead of
marking it DONE; occurrences missed while the app was not running fire once,
not once per missed slot.
.B Skip next
(context menu, Ctrl+K) drops the upcoming occurrence.
To stop a repeating alarm, remove it.
.SS Notes
Text after the time expression becomes the alarm label; the command column
keeps only the time part:
.PP
.RS
.B in 10m stretch
.br
.B in 5m, water plants
.br
.B at 15:10 team call
.RE
.PP
Parentheses and quotes still work:
.BR "in 5m (laundry)" ,
.BR "in 10m \(dqpick up kids\(dq" .
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
Focus the add line.
.TP
.B Enter
Add an alarm from the input line (main window).
.TP
.B F1 / ?
Show the full alarm time syntax (relative, absolute, zones, repeating, notes)
with examples. The
.B ?
button next to the input line does the same.
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
Edit the selected alarm.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Restart the selected alarm (re-evaluate its command from now).
.TP
.B Ctrl+K
Skip the next occurrence of the selected repeating alarm(s).
.TP
.B Delete / Ctrl+D
Remove the selected alarm(s).
.TP
.B Esc
Hide the main window to the tray; in the notification dialog, snooze 5 minutes.
.TP
.B Enter / Space
Acknowledge in the notification dialog.
.SH D-BUS
The primary instance owns a well-known name on the session bus.
Scripting and debugging can use
.B busctl
(or any D-Bus client) instead of the CLI.
.PP
.TS
l l.
Service	org.alarmqt.AlarmQt
Object path	/org/alarmqt/AlarmQt
Interface	org.alarmqt.AlarmQt
.TE
.PP
Methods:
.TP
.B List
Return a multiline string (same format as
.BR \-\-list ).
.TP
.B ListLines
Return one formatted line per alarm as a string array.
.TP
.B Add \fIexpression\fR
Parse and add an alarm.
Returns an empty string on success, or an error message.
.TP
.B Raise
Show and activate the main window.
.TP
.B Quit
Exit the primary instance.
.TP
.B ClearDone
Remove all acknowledged alarms; returns how many were removed.
.TP
.B Version
Return the application version string.
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B busctl \-\-user call org.alarmqt.AlarmQt /org/alarmqt/AlarmQt org.alarmqt.AlarmQt List
.B busctl \-\-user call org.alarmqt.AlarmQt /org/alarmqt/AlarmQt org.alarmqt.AlarmQt ListLines
.B busctl \-\-user call org.alarmqt.AlarmQt /org/alarmqt/AlarmQt org.alarmqt.AlarmQt Add s \(dqin 10m stretch\(dq
.B busctl \-\-user call org.alarmqt.AlarmQt /org/alarmqt/AlarmQt org.alarmqt.AlarmQt Raise
.B busctl \-\-user call org.alarmqt.AlarmQt /org/alarmqt/AlarmQt org.alarmqt.AlarmQt Quit
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/alarmqt/alarms.json
Persistent alarm store (XDG state directory).
Defaults to
.I ~/.local/state/alarmqt/alarms.json
when
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Could not parse an alarm expression given on the command line,
or a D-Bus call to the primary instance failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start or raise the app:
.RS
.B alarmqt
.RE
.TP
Add a relative alarm with a note:
.RS
.B alarmqt \(dqin 10m stretch\(dq
.RE
.TP
Add an absolute alarm:
.RS
.B alarmqt \(dqat 15:10\(dq
.RE
.TP
Add repeating alarms:
.RS
.B alarmqt \(dqevery monday at 18:00 laundry\(dq
.br
.B alarmqt \(dqevery 30m drink water\(dq
.RE
.TP
List alarms (local store or via D-Bus if a primary is running):
.RS
.B alarmqt \-\-list
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR busctl (1),
.UR https://github.com/Grumbel/alarmqt
.UE
